# Build output: where build/build.sh writes.
# (core/ is a submodule, managed by git itself; manifest/modules_gen.go is a generated
# file that **is committed** -- it is the proof of "what this commit installs", see
# tools/distgen.)
/dist/

# Output of the public site: where site/build.sh writes (tools/sitegen's pages plus the demo).
#
# Not a contradiction with web/dist: that one is committed because `//go:embed all:web/dist`
# has to read it for an offline build; nobody needs this one on disk -- the Pages pipeline
# rebuilds it from source every time. Same reasoning as dist/architecture.html: it is the
# product of "this moment", and a stale copy makes people believe the site is like that.
# So it goes into .gitignore.
/site/dist/

# A stray `go build ./tools/distgen` output (the tool is run with `go run`).
/distgen
